-    markdown:
-      "## retrieve_rate_schedule\n\n`client.v1.contracts.rateCards.retrieveRateSchedule(rate_card_id: string, starting_at: string, limit?: number, next_page?: string, ending_before?: string, selectors?: { billing_frequency?: 'MONTHLY' | 'QUARTERLY' | 'ANNUAL' | 'WEEKLY'; partial_pricing_group_values?: object; pricing_group_values?: object; product_id?: string; }[]): { data: object[]; next_page?: string; }`\n\n**post** `/v1/contract-pricing/rate-cards/getRateSchedule`\n\nA rate card defines the prices that you charge for your products. Rate cards support scheduled changes over time, to allow you to easily roll out pricing changes and new product launches across your customer base. Use this endpoint to understand the rate schedule `starting_at` a given date, optionally filtering the list of rates returned based on product id or pricing group values. For example, you may want to display a schedule of upcoming price changes for a given product in your product experience - use this endpoint to fetch that information from its source of truth in Metronome. \n\nIf you want to understand the rates for a specific customer's contract, inclusive of contract-level overrides, use the `getContractRateSchedule` endpoint.\n\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `rate_card_id: string`\n  ID of the rate card to get the schedule for\n\n- `starting_at: string`\n  inclusive starting point for the rates schedule\n\n- `limit?: number`\n  Max number of results that should be returned\n\n- `next_page?: string`\n  Cursor that indicates where the next page of results should start.\n\n- `ending_before?: string`\n  optional exclusive end date for the rates schedule. When not specified rates will show all future schedule segments.\n\n- `selectors?: { billing_frequency?: 'MONTHLY' | 'QUARTERLY' | 'ANNUAL' | 'WEEKLY'; partial_pricing_group_values?: object; pricing_group_values?: object; product_id?: string; }[]`\n  List of rate selectors, rates matching ANY of the selector will be included in the response Passing no selectors will result in all rates being returned.\n\n### Returns\n\n- `{ data: { entitled: boolean; product_custom_fields: object; product_id: string; product_name: string; product_tags: string[]; rate: object; starting_at: string; billing_frequency?: 'MONTHLY' | 'QUARTERLY' | 'ANNUAL' | 'WEEKLY'; commit_rate?: object; ending_before?: string; pricing_group_values?: object; }[]; next_page?: string; }`\n\n  - `data: { entitled: boolean; product_custom_fields: object; product_id: string; product_name: string; product_tags: string[]; rate: { rate_type: 'FLAT' | 'PERCENTAGE' | 'SUBSCRIPTION' | 'CUSTOM' | 'TIERED' | 'TIERED_PERCENTAGE'; credit_type?: object; custom_rate?: object; is_prorated?: boolean; price?: number; pricing_group_values?: object; quantity?: number; tiers?: object[]; }; starting_at: string; billing_frequency?: 'MONTHLY' | 'QUARTERLY' | 'ANNUAL' | 'WEEKLY'; commit_rate?: { rate_type: 'FLAT' | 'PERCENTAGE' | 'SUBSCRIPTION' | 'TIERED' | 'TIERED_PERCENTAGE' | 'CUSTOM'; price?: number; tiers?: object[]; }; ending_before?: string; pricing_group_values?: object; }[]`\n  - `next_page?: string`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport Metronome from '@metronome/sdk';\n\nconst client = new Metronome();\n\nconst response = await client.v1.contracts.rateCards.retrieveRateSchedule({ rate_card_id: 'f3d51ae8-f283-44e1-9933-a3cf9ad7a6fe', starting_at: '2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z' });\n\nconsole.log(response);\n```",
